schema SurfacePresentationCell
generation surface-presentation-cells-1
authority SurfaceIR + AddressPlane + InformationPolicy

field grammar
  type enum[discover,stage,channels,community,board,spatial,listings,inbox,territory,observations,worlds,packs,link,studio,console]
  role interaction-grammar

field presentation_class
  type enum[anonymous,personal,member_worker,operator]
  role presentation-only

field question
  type text
  role human-experience-wording

field experience_character
  type text
  role human-experience-wording

field visible_sections
  type set[text]
  role projection-shape

field preferred_renderers
  type set[text]
  role lowering-preference

field allowed_affordance_families
  type set[text]
  role offered-family-not-authority

field requires
  type set[relation,pack,habitat,work_scope,institution,information_policy]
  role native-closure-input

invariant complete-matrix
  statement each interaction grammar has exactly one cell for each presentation class

invariant presentation-not-standing
  statement a cell describes what a resolved closure can look like; it never supplies actor identity, role, audience, entitlement, provider admission, payment, spend or effect authority

forbidden_inference operator cell -> operator authority
forbidden_inference personal cell -> an actor has a relation, Habitat or Pack closure
forbidden_inference cell change -> a different candidate truth set without a corresponding native closure
